# Every key here is optional: the core runs without any of them.
# Local development: copy this file to .env (git-ignored).
# Hostinger: set the same names in hPanel -> Environment Variables.

# Full ship coverage for Riga, Liepaja, Ventspils and the Gulf of Riga. Free account at https://aisstream.io
# Without it the Ships layer only shows the northern approaches (open Finnish data).
AISSTREAM_API_KEY=

# Briefs written by a language model (Claude). Key from https://platform.claude.com
# Without it the regional brief and the country briefs are written by rules and templates.
# With it, a process that stays up makes at most 81 calls a day: 72 for the regional brief (one
# per 20 minutes, only while somebody has it open) and 9 for the country briefs (one per country,
# once a day). A start that finds the temp folder empty writes all of them again: up to 10 calls
# each time, so on a host that wipes the folder the daily total follows the number of starts.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which model writes the briefs. Default: claude-haiku-4-5, the cheapest and fastest.
# claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-opus-5-5 write better briefs at a higher price per call.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Ceiling on model calls per UTC day, counted by the running process. Default: 120. Past it the
# briefs are written by rules until midnight UTC. 0 switches the model off. The count is kept in
# the temp folder, and a start that finds the folder empty counts from zero: this stops a busy day
# or a bug, not a host that keeps wiping the folder. The cap that holds whatever the host does is
# a spend limit on the key's workspace in the Claude Console.
AI_MAX_CALLS_PER_DAY=
